course: dictionary
lesson: 13666
title: Informative writing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Informative means giving useful facts and knowledge. When a text is informative, it teaches you something true and useful. «The museum guide gave an informative talk about how bees make honey.» The guide taught the listeners real facts, so the talk was informative.
explain: Informative writing, such as a non-chronological report or a leaflet, gives facts to the reader. It is not a story, and it is not just someone's opinion. Good informative texts often have headings, facts and clear explanations that help you find things quickly.
explain: To check if a text is informative, ask yourself: did I learn something true and useful? Words like «for example», «because» and «facts» are clues. Read the text again and look for the facts it gives you.
fact: Informative means giving useful facts and knowledge.
fact: Informative writing gives facts to the reader, not a story or an opinion.
fact: A good informative text has headings, facts and clear explanations.
fact: «An informative talk» is a talk that teaches you something real.
fact: A trip to a museum or a documentary can be very informative.
exercise: «The leaflet about sharks was very informative.» What does informative mean here? | *Giving useful facts and knowledge | Written in a secret code | Short and quick to read | Funny and silly
exercise: Which of these is most likely to be informative writing? | A diary of a birthday party | A story about a dragon | A poem about the moon | *A non-chronological report about penguins, with headings
exercise: «The guide's talk was informative, full of facts about Roman roads.» Find and copy the word that means giving useful facts. | roads | talk | guide | *informative
test: Which sentence is informative? | *«Foxes have thick tails that help them balance when they run.» | «I think foxes are the best animals ever.» | «Once upon a time, a fox met a crow.»
test: Which phrase means a talk that teaches you something real? | *an informative talk | a late talk | a silly talk | a whispered talk
exam: Which is the best reason to call a text informative? | *It gives the reader useful facts about its topic | It uses lots of adjectives | It is very long | It has a funny ending
